<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Load (230)</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>load &lt;unit@zone&gt;
load &lt;unit&gt;
load &lt;player&gt;
</pre>
<p>Examples:
</p>
<pre>load bread@midgaard
load Gnort
</pre>
<p><b>Loading a monster or a thing</b> fetches a fresh one from the world's 
zone files, by its symbolic name: unit@zone, or the name alone for one in 
your own zone. A thing you can carry appears in your inventory ("You 
secretly load ..."); anything else appears in the room, which sees you 
open an interdimensional gate and fetch it, and it says "Hello World!". 
Rooms can't be loaded. Money takes level 254. A zone may demand a 
higher level to load from it (its load level); its creators may load 
from it all the same.
</p><p><b>Loading a player</b> (level 245) brings a player who is not in the game 
into your room, with what they carry, as if they had lost their link: if 
they connect, they step into the character. This is refused if they are 
connected, or already in the game link-dead. Loading a player of a higher 
level than yours is logged.
</p><p>It is logged. To get rid of what you loaded, see <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Purge</a>.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Purge</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Wstat</a>
</pre>




</div>